commit e0189729b1c5536c0d3714fe4219de517df763eb

C03: reassurances and visual requests are never clarified as effects; visual content gets a plain boundary reply (CONVERSATION1345)

CONVERSATION1343 measured: «NO te preocupes si se abrio steam» was turned into a clarification by the effect-shape check before the reassurance shape could answer, and «Tienes algun meme?» came out as «Pido un meme, está fuera de lo que hago» through the generic unsupported anchor (one pair exhausted its retries, another asked which memes).

effect_intent: reassurance_statement and visual_content_noun (shared readers). Mind: a reassurance or a visual-content request keeps its conversation decision (no effect-shape clarification, no unsupported rewrite by that path). Composer: presentation shape visual_content_boundary with its prompt, anchors (the noun asked for) and contract (a plain "cannot show" in the first person, the noun named, no promise, no question).

No .NET change. Offline probe only; tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


